positions.description:
* Created and edited materials for current and prospective international students at the University of Tartu; 
* Maintained and created content for the university’s English-language website;
* Ensured consistency between English-language and Estonian-language webpages and performed translations into English where necessary;
* Used external resources to ensure that information about getting settled in Estonia was relayed clearly and accurately to international students;
* Co-managed a university-wide photo and video contest

* Prepared and delivered presentations about the U.S. higher education system to high school students across Estonia and in Latvia; 
* Represented EducationUSA Tartu at education fairs and other outreach events and did follow-up reporting; 
* Edited EducationUSA Tartu's website, ensured its consistency with the Estonian version and translated missing information where necessary

* Proofread, optimized and distributed client press releases to thousands of media outlets worldwide;
* Fielded high-stakes, time-sensitive customer requests by telephone and email;
* Counseled a diverse client base on communications best practices and gave search engine optimization (SEO) recommendations

* Created, edited, proofread, and translated (Russian to English) materials related to studying abroad in Russia at the Higher School of Economics and the New Economic School; 
* Proofread scholarly articles written by non-native English speakers virtually and face-to-face;
* Held one-on-one English writing consultations with Russian students;
* Created presentations and guides on subjects such as how to write a motivation letter and how to write letters of recommendation

